  "notes": [
    "Initial owned-tree taskkill returned 128 for already-exited WebView descendants; cleanup now verifies root exit and preserves the original failure.",
    "Initial cargo release omitted custom-protocol; renderer IPC was rejected. All authoritative native evidence uses the packaged-protocol release.",
    "Cold hidden WebView selection exceeded 15 seconds; only startup readiness uses a bounded 45-second deadline. No performance gate was reclassified.",
    "Native playlist opening exposed the synchronous WebView2 constructor deadlock. The command is now async and constructs off the event thread; the native playlist flow verifies the fix.",
    "The first playlist assertion assumed history was source-ordered. History is newest-first; membership is compared by URL while native FIFO/concurrency remain checked.",
    "Peek fixture cursor initially lay at the compact bottom edge. An ongoing temporary timer bootstraps the lazy view before starting link exposure, is dismissed before capture, and Peek paint ownership/geometry are explicitly awaited.",
    "Font audit now targets the rendered strong text node. Playwright clipping reset DPR; raw CDP plus PNG header assertions prove actual 2x output. No raster normalization, resampling or tolerant repeat checks were used.",
    "Site checks caught stale OG CSS provenance, an old M3 geometry assertion, and a mobile absolute-caption contrast incomplete. OG was rendered again, HEAD baseline geometry was measured, and the mobile caption now reserves space on an opaque token background. No scanner exception was added.",
    "Legacy restart used DB existence plus a fixed sleep. It now waits for the owned command consumer before unchanged action deadlines. Evidence export uses List.ToArray to avoid a PowerShell binder error after all assertions passed.",
    "The first legacy progress predicate used five separate Python/SQLite reads across a short run. One SQL snapshot preserves all status/progress/speed/ETA/concurrency conditions."
  ]
}
